{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/pulls/229","id":4055565320,"node_id":"PR_kwDOCaGR_c7xuwQI","html_url":"https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/pull/229","diff_url":"https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/pull/229.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/pull/229.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/issues/229","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/pulls/229/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/pulls/229/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/issues/229/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/electron-userland/electron-installer-common/statuses/3a71dd08ba4739d2b521d3cb1023bfd5f8b0e4b1","number":229,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat!: rewrite in TypeScript as an ES module","user":{"login":"erickzhao","id":16010076,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MDEwMDc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16010076?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao","html_url":"https://github.com/erickzhao","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erickzhao/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nSecond PR in the stack splitting up #226 (follows #227, now merged). This is the large, unavoidably-coupled change: the TypeScript/ESM rewrite and the Vitest migration ship together, because the new test suite is written in ESM/TypeScript against the ESM/TypeScript source.\n\n- **TypeScript + ESM**: rewrites all sources from CommonJS JS to TypeScript, emitting ESM to `dist/` via `tsc` (`exports` map, `\"type\": \"module\"`). **Breaking**: the package is now ESM-only and can no longer be `require()`d.\n- **Slimmer deps**: drops `fs-extra`, `glob`, `lodash`, `tmp-promise`, `parse-author`, and `@malept/cross-spawn-promise` in favor of Node built-ins + a small `spawn` helper; templating now uses `ejs`.\n- **Vitest**: migrates the suite from ava → Vitest (incl. type-level tests), drops `nyc`/`tsd`/`codecov`.\n- **oxlint/oxfmt**: replaces ESLint + Standard with type-aware oxlint and oxfmt; adds a Husky `pre-commit` hook running lint-staged.\n- **CI**: adds a `build` step before lint/test.\n\n`@electron/asar` intentionally stays at v3 here — the v4 (ESM-only) bump is the next PR in the stack.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `yarn build` — compiles clean\n- [x] `yarn lint` — oxfmt + type-aware oxlint pass\n- [x] `yarn test` — 79 tests pass, no type errors\n- [ ] CI passes on all three platforms\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <svc-devxp-claude@slack-corp.com>","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-14T20:20:57Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T20:32:14Z","closed_at":"2026-07-14T20:32:12Z","merged_at":"2026-07-14T20:32:12Z","merge_commit_sha":"eed7647f13eda976a55ef46750c5d352b1f94983","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dsanders11","id":5820654,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MjA2NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5820654?v=4","gravatar_id":"",